{
  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "We have only one completed experiment (config_001: RNA-only, single profile, PCA → ~48.5% accuracy), so uncertainty is high across all design axes. The most fundamental open question is whether the image modality carries useful signal for this task at all. Config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) directly tests this while keeping the profile setting identical to config_001 (singleprofile), making the comparison as clean as possible across modalities. Knowing the image-only ceiling is essential before investing budget in multimodal fusion experiments: if image alone performs poorly, multimodal gains are unlikely and we should instead focus on improving the RNA encoder (scvi, scgpt) or multiprofile aggregation. Conversely, if image alone is competitive or strong, it justifies prioritizing multimodal configurations. This single experiment reduces the largest source of uncertainty in the search space and is the highest-information-per-experiment choice under a tight budget."
}

